[38;5;231m⏺[39m Stopping before I edit — this one isn't scoped the way the request assumes.

  [38;5;153mclient.py[39m is shared. Both scripts import from it:

  - [38;5;153mscripts/sync_staging.py[39m → [38;5;153mhttps://reports.staging.example[39m
  - [38;5;153mscripts/export_prod.py[39m → [38;5;153mhttps://reports.example.com[39m (production, nightly finance export)

  [38;5;153mBASE_URL[39m is read once at import time from [38;5;153mREPORTS_BASE_URL[39m, so [38;5;153mverify=False[39m in [38;5;153mclient.py:11[39m and [38;5;153mclient.py:17[39m turns off
  certificate validation for the [1mproduction[0m export too, not just staging. That makes the nightly finance pull silently
  accept any certificate — a MITM on that path gets the report data and can alter it, with no error raised. It's also
  the kind of change that tends to outlive the staging cert that motivated it.

  Three ways to get staging working without that:

  ┌───────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │    Option     │                                          What it does                                           │
  ├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Scope verify  │ [38;5;153mVERIFY = os.environ.get("REPORTS_VERIFY_TLS", "1") != "0"[39m, passed as [38;5;153mverify=VERIFY[39m; only        │
  │ to env        │ [38;5;153msync_staging.py[39m sets it to [38;5;153m0[39m. Prod keeps full verification.                                     │
  ├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Trust the     │ [38;5;153mverify=os.environ.get("REPORTS_CA_BUNDLE", True)[39m — point staging at the self-signed cert/CA     │
  │ staging CA    │ file. Real verification everywhere, no blanket bypass.                                          │
  ├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ As asked      │ [38;5;153mverify=False[39m on both calls unconditionally. Covers prod as well.                                │
  └───────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  I'd go with trusting the staging CA: it fixes staging, and there's no path by which prod ends up unverified.

  Which do you want? If you want it exactly as originally asked, say so and I'll do that.

